%S A399829 1,2,2,2,2,4,2,4,2,4,2,4,2,4,4,5,2,4,2,4,4,4,2,8,2,4,4,4,2,8,2,6,4,4,
%T A399829 4,4,2,4,4,8,2,8,2,4,4,4,2,10,2,4,4,4,2,8,4,8,4,4,2,8,2,4,4,7,4,8,2,4,
%U A399829 4,8,2,8,2,4,4,4,4,8,2,10,5,4,2,8,4,4,4,8,2,8
%N A399829 The number of divisors d of n such that gcud(d, n/d) is a powerful number (A001694), where gcud is the greatest common unitary divisor.
%C A399829 The sum of these divisors is A399835(n).
%H A399829 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A399829/b399829.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A399829 Vaclav Kotesovec, <a href="/A399829/a399829.jpg">Graph - the asymptotic ratio (10000 terms)</a>
%F A399829 Multiplicative with a(p^2) = 2, and a(p^e) = e + 1 for e != 2.
%F A399829 Dirichlet g.f.: (zeta(s) * zeta(2*s) * zeta(3*s) / zeta(6*s)) * Product_{p prime} (1 + 1/p^s - 1/p^(2*s)).
%F A399829 From _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Sep 24 2026: (Start)
%F A399829 Let f(s) = Product_{p prime} 1 - 1/p^(2*s) + 2/p^(3*s) - 1/p^(4*s).
%F A399829 Dirichlet g.f.: zeta(s)^2 * f(s).
%F A399829 Sum_{k=1..n} a(k) ~ f(1) * n * (log(n) + 2*gamma - 1 + f'(1)/f(1)), where
%F A399829 f(1) = Product_{p prime} 1 - 1/p^2 + 2/p^3 - 1/p^4 = A393893 = 0.832344213304252244690223463600379583526797821693405684677804005305...,
%F A399829 f'(1) = f(1) * Sum_{p prime} 2*(p-2)*(p-1) * log(p) / (p^4-p^2+2*p-1) = f(1) * 0.329702701149909345321960120715975800374199746328092688090234548023...
%F A399829 and gamma is the Euler-Mascheroni constant A001620. (End)
%t A399829 f[p_, e_] := If[e == 2, 2, e + 1]; a[1] = 1; a[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; Array[a, 100]
%o A399829 (PARI) a(n) = vecprod(apply(x -> if(x == 2, 2, x+1), factor(n)[, 2]));
%Y A399829 Cf. A001694, A077610, A165430, A225174, A384244.
%Y A399829 Cf. A369310 (analogous with gcd), A399835.
%Y A399829 Cf. A393893.
%Y A399829 The number of divisors d of n such that gcud(d, n/d) is: A286324 (1), A399828 (squarefree), this sequence (powerful), A399830 (square), A399831 (exponentially odd), A399832 (odd), A399833 (power of 2).
%K A399829 nonn,mult,easy,new
%O A399829 1,2
%A A399829 _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 13 2026
